 4. Mapped: Death penalty differences 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data : Death Penalty Information Center. (New Hampshire abolished the death penalty but retains one prisoner on death row.) Map: Erin Davis/Axios Visuals Lethal injections are under scrutiny after Christa Pike survived two rounds of drugs during Tennessee's failed attempt to execute her.

 It's been the dominant U.S. execution method for decades, accounting for roughly 89% of the 1,683 executions carried out since 1976, Axios' Herb Scribner writes. Where things stand: Pike is in critical condition and receiving "lifesaving care" at a hospital, AP reports . 

 The failed execution led Republican Gov. Bill Lee to order a review and to indefinitely postpone Pike's execution and Tennessee's lone other one scheduled for this year. The 50-year-old was sentenced to death for a murder she committed in 1995 at age 18. She would have been the first woman executed in Tennessee in more than 200 years. Share this map . 

 
 
