 5. Trump&#x27;s TIME record 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Left: President Trump's first TIME cover, from Jan. 16, 1989 (age 42). Right: His latest, 37 years later, photographed by Dan Winters on Sept. 2 (age 80).

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 President Trump is back on the cover of TIME — his 56th appearance, edging out Richard Nixon for the most ever.

 The president sat for 75 minutes in the Oval Office on Monday with senior correspondent Eric Cortellessa and editor-in-chief Sam Jacobs. What Trump said: 

 🇮🇱 If he'd back Netanyahu in this month's Israeli elections: "Well, I can only say that I'm not involved in politics anymore, except that we're popular." He didn't answer two more direct questions. ✍️ On pardoning his staff members: "Yeah, sure I'd do that. ... Well, Sleepy Joe Biden, he gave pardons to everyone." ⚖️ On his SCOTUS appointments: "I gave them the position of a lifetime ... and they voted against me often. ... I do like loyalty, yeah." Check out the cover story ... Read the transcript . 

 
 
