 6. 📈 Mortgage rates keep rising 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data : Freddie Mac; Chart: Pete Gannon/Axios Mortgage rates spiked to their highest level in nearly three years yesterday, continuing their climb above the 7% threshold, Axios' Nathan Bomey writes .

 😨 They've climbed 0.25 points in just the last week — and they're up almost a full point from a year ago. That means mortgage applications are plunging.

 The Mortgage Bankers Association reported that applications during the week ended Sept. 25 fell 6% from the prior week. Share this chart . 

 
 
