 7. 🍿 Buzzy Holmes doc 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Photo: A24 New York's hottest ticket this week — the N.Y. Times reports some people waited in a standby line for almost 16 hours! — was to catch the second-ever screening of A24's "You Can See Everything" at the New York Film Festival.

 The documentary, by Nathan Fielder and Lance Oppenheim, is an all-access look at the days before Theranos founder Elizabeth Holmes reported to federal prison on fraud charges. Fielder told those lucky enough to get in that his time in Holmes' home was disorienting: "I had this weird experience where she seemed so genuine at times, but also clocking — tracking my thoughts — that she's a liar."

 "I am still struggling to this day to understand what I went through," he told The Hollywood Reporter . Watch the trailer . 

 
 
