 8. 🦅 Before you fly: Pigeon patrol 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Photo: Omer Urer/Anadolu via Getty Images

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 The Massachusetts Bay Transportation Authority thinks one way to stop pigeons from pooping all over its property is to have trained birds of prey ready to swoop in and regulate.

 The MBTA is asking falconry companies how raptors could help keep birds out of a system with more than 200 rapid transit and commuter rail stations, Axios Boston 's Mike Deehan reports. 🐦 The T's current defenses against the winged rats are mostly just netting and spikes.

 A pigeon-trapping pilot has launched. Share this story ... Subscribe to Axios Local , now in 43 cities. 

 
 
